CHMOD
=====

Change file permissions.


BASIC
-----
chmod +x file.sh

Makes file executable.


PERMISSION SYMBOLS
------------------
+               Add permission
-               Remove permission
x               Execute
r               Read
w               Write


EXAMPLES
--------
chmod +x script.sh      Make executable
chmod -x file.txt       Remove execute
chmod +r file.txt       Make readable
chmod -w file.txt       Remove write


NUMERIC MODE
------------
chmod 755 file

4 = read
2 = write
1 = execute

755 = rwx r-x r-x
644 = rw- r-- r--
700 = rwx --- ---


RECURSIVE
---------
chmod -R +x folder

Apply to folder and all contents.


WHEN TO USE
-----------
• Make shell scripts executable
• Protect sensitive files
• Grant access to others


COMMON
------
chmod 755 script.sh     Executable script
chmod 644 file.txt      Regular file
chmod 700 secret.txt    Private file
